{#
    Circulation Badge -- one-line standing of an item on the shared shelf

    Renders how many physical copies of an item exist, how many are free right now, and
    how many members are queued for it, as Bulma chips. When the viewer holds one of the
    copies that fact replaces the availability chip, because it is the only one they act
    on. Renders nothing when the item has no copies, so a list cell can call it
    unconditionally.

    Used in:    App\Twig\CirculationExtension::badge, called as circulation_badge() from
                item list cells and item detail headers
    Parameters:
        - summary (App\Circulation\Summary, required) -- copy counts and the viewer's position
#}
<span class="tags circulation-badge">
    {% if summary.viewerHolds %}
        <span class="tag is-info is-light">{{ 'circulation.badge_with_you'|trans }}</span>
    {% elseif summary.isAnyAvailable %}
        <span class="tag is-success is-light">{{ 'circulation.badge_available'|trans({'%available%': summary.availableCopies, '%total%': summary.totalCopies}) }}</span>
    {% else %}
        <span class="tag is-light">{{ 'circulation.badge_on_loan'|trans({'%total%': summary.totalCopies}) }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% if summary.queueLength > 0 %}
        <span class="tag is-warning is-light">{{ 'circulation.badge_waiting'|trans({'%count%': summary.queueLength}) }}</span>
    {% endif %}
</span>
